    <string-array name="tips">
        <item>Take photos in daylight, but out of harsh direct sun. Shade gives the clearest colours.</item>
        <item>Fill the square with a single leaf. Several leaves at once confuse the check.</item>
        <item>Pick a leaf that shows the problem clearly, not one that is dead and dry.</item>
        <item>Hold the phone still and tap the screen to focus before taking the photo.</item>
        <item>Check a few different plants. One sick leaf doesn\'t always mean a sick field.</item>
        <item>Remove and destroy badly infected plants early to stop diseases spreading.</item>
        <item>Clean your tools after working with sick plants so you don\'t carry disease to healthy ones.</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="retake_tips">
        <item>Use daylight or shade, not a dark room or harsh sun</item>
        <item>Get closer so one leaf fills the square</item>
        <item>Use a plain background, like your hand or the ground</item>
        <item>Hold steady so the photo is sharp</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="privacy_points">
        <item>Leaf photos are checked on your phone. They are never uploaded.</item>
        <item>Your history is stored only on this phone. Delete it any time.</item>
        <item>The internet is only used to download crop models and updates.</item>
        <item>We don\'t ask for your name, phone number or location.</item>
    </string-array>

